                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "533f75f7-76e0-34f9-8e94-4a8fbaf34c40",
                        "entry_id": "ff38cdb3-886c-3cf4-9341-c9af11ffe37f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "te veel woorden gebruiken voor een mededeling en daardoor saai, vervelend en slaapverwekkend worden"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "39b24fbb-3a28-448b-8718-f96d21af976f",
                                "sense_id": "533f75f7-76e0-34f9-8e94-4a8fbaf34c40",
                                "text": "Inhoudelijk geeft het stuk hen een aantal rake oneliners en observaties in handen, al is de tekst van Den Tex ook wat wijdlopig. Want dat er én een relatiecrisis én een ongeneeslijke ziekte én geloofsdiscussies met een vrome moslim (Ruben de Goede) aan te pas moeten komen om Jans eigen overtuigingen (misschien?) te laten wankelen, voelt uiteindelijk toch wat geforceerd."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5446355c-838e-4ca8-8b31-54e8130024d7",
                                "sense_id": "533f75f7-76e0-34f9-8e94-4a8fbaf34c40",
                                "text": "Regisseur Gary Ross, eerder verantwoordelijk voor de eerste Hunger games-film, baseerde Free state of Jones op historische feiten. Heel veel historische feiten zelfs, iets wat hij met oude foto’s en flinke sprongen in de tijd onderstreept. Dat haalt niet alleen de vaart uit het verhaal, het wordt er ook nogal lang en wijdlopig door."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2f5bd5c9-cbe3-45c0-bc31-b14da712afee",
                        "source_entry_id": "ff38cdb3-886c-3cf4-9341-c9af11ffe37f",
                        "source_sense_id": "533f75f7-76e0-34f9-8e94-4a8fbaf34c40",
                        "target_lang_word": "elaborate",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "elaborate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "238c611e-bf93-3c05-ba1f-b973878181a8",
                                        "entry_id": "b47c6605-26ff-30fc-8c7c-f711eb171e18",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Complex, detailed, or sophisticated."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c783e8b-c7d4-4266-9657-fbac454e4d2f",
                                                "sense_id": "238c611e-bf93-3c05-ba1f-b973878181a8",
                                                "text": "After reading a long, elaborate description, I was impressed but no wiser."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "19dcf582-ad2d-3ddd-9135-5f6c55f0ff64",
                                        "entry_id": "b47c6605-26ff-30fc-8c7c-f711eb171e18",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Intricate, fancy, flashy, or showy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "226d0323-e8b7-469e-9133-fa439a37cddf",
                                                "sense_id": "19dcf582-ad2d-3ddd-9135-5f6c55f0ff64",
                                                "text": "I stared for hours at the elaborate pattern in the rug."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5301af23-3a28-498e-bb01-78232ec3ab28",
                                                "sense_id": "19dcf582-ad2d-3ddd-9135-5f6c55f0ff64",
                                                "text": "The house was a big elaborate limestone affair, evidently new. Winter sunshine sparkled on lace-hung casement, on glass marquise, and the burnished bronze foliations of grille and door."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "elaborate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7b5575e4-6e71-34f0-946b-cbffc6946819",
                                        "entry_id": "e8f80a15-ab4d-3a35-8f65-f7897d33e4b5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Тo develop in detail or complexity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46fc8c8f-8080-4354-be27-ae0ca585fffd",
                                                "sense_id": "7b5575e4-6e71-34f0-946b-cbffc6946819",
                                                "text": "[…] by the time of the subsequent coronation, when the Prussian king put the crown on his own head in child-like belief of the obsolete doctrine called divine right, the untiring statesman had elaborated his scheme of reform."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2adf324c-712f-43b0-8a64-09e0a156be70",
                                                "sense_id": "7b5575e4-6e71-34f0-946b-cbffc6946819",
                                                "text": "The notion of blood purity was first elaborated in Europe, where it was used to separate Old Christians from Spain’s New Christians—women and men of Jewish and Muslim origin whose ancestors had converted to Christianity."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9381ba79-4d1f-328c-b53b-a9c83f05c3d8",
                                        "entry_id": "e8f80a15-ab4d-3a35-8f65-f7897d33e4b5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To expand/enlarge in detail."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "sometimes"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd780278-81de-4d7d-990b-fd29f040f4d0",
                                                "sense_id": "9381ba79-4d1f-328c-b53b-a9c83f05c3d8",
                                                "text": "What do you mean you didn't come home last night? Would you care to elaborate?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f036c18-2406-408c-9b67-44397aee91c6",
                                                "sense_id": "9381ba79-4d1f-328c-b53b-a9c83f05c3d8",
                                                "text": "Could you elaborate on the plot for your novel for me?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d83aa14a-5b5f-4494-a551-762a3677ff93",
                        "source_entry_id": "ff38cdb3-886c-3cf4-9341-c9af11ffe37f",
                        "source_sense_id": "533f75f7-76e0-34f9-8e94-4a8fbaf34c40",
                        "target_lang_word": "extensive",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "extensive",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "00ea8aae-7539-366d-a94d-3206e4d3adeb",
                                        "entry_id": "402e5021-de21-3fca-a7e5-372816cf313b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having a great extent; covering a large area; vast."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b759c0e-c6e6-4454-81c3-3859779ad70c",
                                                "sense_id": "00ea8aae-7539-366d-a94d-3206e4d3adeb",
                                                "text": "In the second century of the Christian era, the Empire of Rome comprehended the fairest part of the earth, and the most civilised portion of mankind. The frontiers of that extensive monarchy were guarded by ancient renown and disciplined valour."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8b093ec7-25e5-32d9-b5bd-98ddad78341c",
                                        "entry_id": "402e5021-de21-3fca-a7e5-372816cf313b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Considerable in amount."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d98eae79-c35a-4473-9229-60e44e5121dd",
                                                "sense_id": "8b093ec7-25e5-32d9-b5bd-98ddad78341c",
                                                "text": "I have done extensive research on the subject."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cc4d6802-d564-3be6-a89a-2b1f4b86f90a",
                                        "entry_id": "402e5021-de21-3fca-a7e5-372816cf313b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Serving to extend or lengthen; characterized by extension."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55b4084a-8600-49e7-9616-cc40d00255ec",
                                                "sense_id": "cc4d6802-d564-3be6-a89a-2b1f4b86f90a",
                                                "text": "For station is properly no rest, but one kind of motion, relating unto that which physicians (from Galen) do name extensive or tonical; that is, an extension of the muscles and organs of motion, maintaining the body at length, or in its proper figure."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b1a87b82-4855-3beb-be15-e8b093955f96",
                                        "entry_id": "402e5021-de21-3fca-a7e5-372816cf313b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having a combined system entropy that equals the sum of the entropies of the independent systems."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b2bd2ad-3f6a-4962-bb86-58b7c57ec118",
                                                "sense_id": "b1a87b82-4855-3beb-be15-e8b093955f96",
                                                "text": "According to Tsallis (1988), the entropy was extensive for T = 1, superextensive for t < 1 and subextensive for t > 1."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e9c4855d-6f02-4fd9-8857-2ed44d366123",
                        "source_entry_id": "ff38cdb3-886c-3cf4-9341-c9af11ffe37f",
                        "source_sense_id": "533f75f7-76e0-34f9-8e94-4a8fbaf34c40",
                        "target_lang_word": "tedious",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tedious",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "949dfc7c-6a20-3ca6-8aca-f4e1b44b1efe",
                                        "entry_id": "e59ca282-f508-32fb-a239-81b0e0447c98",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Boring, monotonous, time-consuming, wearisome, livelong."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9825084a-b558-4618-b7db-29a45b81fd32",
                                                "sense_id": "949dfc7c-6a20-3ca6-8aca-f4e1b44b1efe",
                                                "text": "But in the mean time […] it looks all ſo like ſubterfuge and inveagling; it is ſo nauſeating and teadious a task, that no man thinks he ovvs the Author ſo much ſervice as to find out the reaſon of his ovvn Categoricalneſs for him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c99c2088-f1ae-4999-9995-5f134e52f40d",
                                                "sense_id": "949dfc7c-6a20-3ca6-8aca-f4e1b44b1efe",
                                                "text": "However, upon a ſtrict Review, I blotted out ſeveral Paſſages of leſs Moment which were in my firſt Copy, for fear of being cenſured as tedious and trifling, whereof Travellers are often, perhaps not without Juſtice, accuſed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85ea0ed2-fb56-43fc-b6b5-a286ee3bb472",
                                                "sense_id": "949dfc7c-6a20-3ca6-8aca-f4e1b44b1efe",
                                                "text": "John Gilpin's ſpouse ſaid to her dear, / Though wedded we have been / Theſe twice ten tedious years, yet we / No holiday have ſeen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7253f2c1-261d-4aca-b98a-8e0a16a27d02",
                                                "sense_id": "949dfc7c-6a20-3ca6-8aca-f4e1b44b1efe",
                                                "text": "[pages 24–25] The very fact that these commonplace authors are never more than half-conscious when they write, would be enough to account for their dulness of mind and the tedious things they produce. […] [page 26] The other kind of tediousness is only relative: a reader may find a work dull because he has no interest in the question treated of in it, and this means that his intellect is restricted. The best work may, therefore, be tedious subjectively, tedious, I mean, to this or that particular person; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f18e4b48-a562-4bfd-8fee-de7efdbc7537",
                        "source_entry_id": "ff38cdb3-886c-3cf4-9341-c9af11ffe37f",
                        "source_sense_id": "533f75f7-76e0-34f9-8e94-4a8fbaf34c40",
                        "target_lang_word": "lengthy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "lengthy",
